WEBVTT

01:03.368 --> 01:05.734
[Yeonhyang Temple Food Experience, 2013]

01:31.015 --> 01:33.576
[The late Lady, Joo Kyung Hee]

01:38.344 --> 01:41.850
Mom, the air's nice up here.

02:00.643 --> 02:04.446
Hey! Please untie me! Hurry!

02:04.446 --> 02:05.537
What are you doing?

02:05.537 --> 02:07.743
Please untie me already!

02:07.743 --> 02:09.730
I need to get out of here!

02:09.730 --> 02:10.957
Mom!

02:10.957 --> 02:12.967
- I need to get out of here!
- Mom!

02:12.967 --> 02:15.136
Let me go!

02:15.136 --> 02:18.049
What are you doing?

02:18.049 --> 02:19.369
No!

02:19.369 --> 02:21.227
No!

02:28.694 --> 02:31.845
If you jump from there,
you'll just inconvenience people.

02:33.714 --> 02:36.352
The hiking trail's right below you.

02:36.352 --> 02:40.002
Man, it must've taken a lot
to climb all the way up here.

02:40.002 --> 02:44.043
Why not use that same willpower
to keep living instead?

02:44.043 --> 02:48.168
Just enjoy the fresh air and head down.
The way down's a lot nicer anyway.

03:05.823 --> 03:09.056
I think the buses stopped running.

03:09.886 --> 03:12.604
Seriously? No way...

03:12.604 --> 03:14.444
Where are you headed?

03:14.444 --> 03:15.538
I'll give you a ride.

03:15.538 --> 03:17.859
I'm not getting in a car with a guy
who almost jumped off a cliff.

03:17.859 --> 03:19.224
That's terrifying.

03:19.224 --> 03:21.382
No thanks.

03:22.070 --> 03:24.280
Fair point.

03:26.184 --> 03:28.434
Hey.

03:28.434 --> 03:30.746
Let's meet again sometime. Alive.

03:47.373 --> 03:50.924
Hello, I'm Lee Tae Kwon, one of the new hires.

03:50.924 --> 03:53.370
Looking forward to working with you all.

03:55.327 --> 03:56.537
And lastly,

03:56.537 --> 04:02.144
Joo In Ah here actually came in first
in this recruitment round.

04:02.144 --> 04:03.654
Total elite.

04:03.654 --> 04:05.159
I'll do my best to live up to it.

04:05.159 --> 04:06.783
Looking forward to working with you.

04:06.783 --> 04:08.592
Thank you.

04:25.874 --> 04:29.174
Why are you two so quiet?

04:30.639 --> 04:34.218
In Ah, you should pour Manager Jeon a drink.

04:34.218 --> 04:36.112
Oh, okay.

05:01.293 --> 05:04.050
I heard you're the Haemu Group prince.

05:04.050 --> 05:07.163
The legendary third-gen chaebol himself.

05:09.060 --> 05:13.099
Then I guess you also heard
I'm not exactly royalty.

05:15.466 --> 05:17.204
So...

05:17.204 --> 05:19.949
that's what made life so hard for you
back then?

05:21.783 --> 05:23.399
Anyway, let's work well together.

05:23.399 --> 05:25.695
Manager Jeon Jae Yeol.

05:32.878 --> 05:35.222
I really hoped I'd see you again.

05:36.632 --> 05:39.112
Good thing I stayed alive.

05:49.704 --> 05:51.653
What do you mean?

05:51.653 --> 05:55.055
Jae Yeol handled this project
from the very beginning.

05:55.055 --> 05:58.019
All that's left is the signature,
and now you're taking his credit away?

05:58.019 --> 06:01.679
In Ah, read the room.

06:01.679 --> 06:06.846
Ever since Jeon Seong Yeol joined,
they've been funneling all the wins his way.

06:06.846 --> 06:10.002
So what? That makes it okay?

06:10.658 --> 06:13.451
- If the Chairman finds out...
- Come on.

06:13.451 --> 06:17.464
This only works because
the Chairman's letting it happen.

06:19.183 --> 06:20.940
You heard about

06:20.940 --> 06:22.553
Jeon Jae Yeol's mother too, right?

06:22.553 --> 06:24.270
People think he has limitations.

06:24.270 --> 06:27.520
That's why everyone's siding
with the second son no matter what.

06:27.520 --> 06:30.135
Go to Dubai and close the deal.
There's a flight in two hours.

06:30.135 --> 06:33.110
- Seriously, you need to hurry.
- In Ah.

06:33.110 --> 06:35.936
You're going to get yourself in trouble.

06:35.936 --> 06:39.348
And this isn't my project.

06:39.348 --> 06:41.761
It's the company's project.

06:42.607 --> 06:44.285
Still, this is so unfair.

06:44.285 --> 06:47.654
You did all the work.

06:47.654 --> 06:50.161
It's enough that you know that.

06:57.044 --> 07:01.867
They're seriously the worst.
Every single one of them.

07:01.867 --> 07:03.727
In Ah.

07:06.747 --> 07:08.660
I'm going to

07:09.434 --> 07:12.297
protect you in this company.

07:12.297 --> 07:15.303
Come hell or high water,

07:17.387 --> 07:20.293
I'm standing by you, Jeon Jae Yeol.

07:25.460 --> 07:28.223
This pisses me off.

07:41.095 --> 07:43.323
So... you two used to date.

07:44.976 --> 07:47.543
Yeah. We did.

07:50.196 --> 07:52.403
Why'd you break up?

07:53.162 --> 07:54.954
Well...

07:54.954 --> 07:58.600
He found someone more suitable for his world,

07:58.600 --> 08:00.930
and I wanted to live my own life.

08:00.930 --> 08:03.017
Same old story.

08:03.017 --> 08:04.901
It's all in the past.

08:05.717 --> 08:07.479
You sure about that?

08:08.534 --> 08:10.455
What do you mean?

08:18.037 --> 08:20.062
We got a tip.

08:20.062 --> 08:23.555
That you were involved
in an inappropriate relationship at work.

08:23.555 --> 08:27.321
Those photos were of you two, huh?
You and the Vice Chairman.

08:54.386 --> 08:55.613
You came.

08:55.613 --> 08:57.665
It's been a while,

08:57.665 --> 08:59.110
Vice Chairman.

09:03.584 --> 09:06.004
I missed you.

09:08.916 --> 09:12.319
It was the day he came back from overseas.

09:12.319 --> 09:15.619
It was just a hug after seeing him again.
It meant nothing.

09:17.990 --> 09:20.495
"It meant nothing?"

09:20.495 --> 09:25.657
That's not really what I saw back there.

09:26.861 --> 09:30.766
Are those feelings one-sided
on the Vice Chairman's part?

09:30.766 --> 09:32.414
Or do you two

09:33.082 --> 09:35.742
still have feelings for each other?

10:02.453 --> 10:05.626
I'd appreciate it if you stopped
showing up uninvited.

10:07.698 --> 10:08.728
In Ah.

10:08.728 --> 10:09.992
Let go.

10:10.904 --> 10:12.865
Let go!

10:18.605 --> 10:23.551
The Vice Chairman and I are just coworkers.

10:23.551 --> 10:25.491
Nothing more, nothing less.

10:25.491 --> 10:28.357
I don't have feelings for him anymore.

10:34.614 --> 10:37.272
Honestly, after we got the tip,
I was suspicious.

10:37.272 --> 10:40.436
So I looked into you, followed you around,

10:40.436 --> 10:42.915
even staked out your place.

10:45.793 --> 10:47.266
Figures.

10:47.266 --> 10:48.768
Living up to your reputation as Audit's Ace.

10:48.768 --> 10:52.458
Didn't expect it to be the Vice Chairman,
though.

10:53.579 --> 10:55.266
So?

10:56.522 --> 10:59.860
What's your conclusion as the PM lead?

11:09.186 --> 11:11.040
I don't know.

11:12.473 --> 11:15.229
I want to believe

11:15.229 --> 11:17.803
everything you said.

11:18.593 --> 11:20.404
That you two are over.

11:20.404 --> 11:23.690
No matter how he feels,

11:23.690 --> 11:26.381
you don't have feelings for him anymore.

11:26.381 --> 11:27.750
But maybe

11:29.041 --> 11:32.374
that's just me wanting to believe that.

11:37.882 --> 11:40.533
Just give me some time.

11:40.533 --> 11:43.246
I'll try to think about this objectively.

12:29.109 --> 12:32.929
[Episode 7: To Her Lover]

12:37.056 --> 12:39.346
- Five soju glasses.
- Five soju glasses.

12:39.346 --> 12:42.106
- And five paper cups too.
- Five.

12:42.106 --> 12:44.703
- Two spoons.
- Oh, sparkling water.

12:44.703 --> 12:46.013
Sparkling water?

12:46.013 --> 12:47.400
- Didn't add that.
- For highballs.

12:47.400 --> 12:50.194
Okay. Add sparkling water too, please.

12:50.194 --> 12:51.941
Yeah, and...

12:51.941 --> 12:56.021
Sir, why do you keep pacing around?
I'm already losing my mind here.

12:56.021 --> 12:59.398
You know, it's our first workshop in forever.

12:59.398 --> 13:01.229
I was thinking,

13:01.229 --> 13:04.509
this workshop really needs some barbecue.

13:04.509 --> 13:06.186
Otherwise it'll feel kind of lame.

13:06.186 --> 13:08.908
- Don't you think so, White Blood Cell?
- Yes, it would be a little disappointing.

13:08.908 --> 13:09.575
- Right?
- Yeah.

13:09.575 --> 13:10.750
Unnie,

13:10.750 --> 13:13.884
11 people are driving themselves,
and everyone else is taking the bus.

13:13.884 --> 13:15.134
Okay.

13:15.134 --> 13:17.858
Then send that list to the driver.

13:17.858 --> 13:19.015
Got it.

13:19.015 --> 13:22.343
Since when were you two on "unnie" terms?

13:22.343 --> 13:24.296
Funny what you pick up on.

13:24.296 --> 13:26.526
Did you finish everything you needed to do?

13:26.526 --> 13:27.866
Why are you still here?

13:27.866 --> 13:30.055
Did you text the whole Audit team or not?

13:30.055 --> 13:33.401
I'm doing it now, unnie. Quit nagging already.

13:33.401 --> 13:37.125
Hae Young, I really think we need
whole pork belly or pork neck.

13:37.125 --> 13:38.895
- Okay, okay.
- Should we buy some then?

13:38.895 --> 13:42.698
- I'll get pork neck.
- Great, buy the whole cut.

14:07.512 --> 14:10.939
Assistant Manager Noh Ki Jun, was it?

14:10.939 --> 14:12.716
Can he be trusted?

14:12.716 --> 14:14.734
He seemed pretty cocky.

14:16.612 --> 14:19.734
Yeah, he's definitely not the obedient type.

14:20.872 --> 14:22.782
What did he mean earlier?

14:22.782 --> 14:24.806
"The thing you call impossible,
it's not so impossible after all."

14:24.806 --> 14:27.123
What was impossible again...

14:27.123 --> 14:29.182
and what wasn't?

14:30.754 --> 14:33.358
Why is the Vice Chairman of Haemu Group

14:33.358 --> 14:35.577
so interested in some random assistant manager?

14:35.577 --> 14:38.222
Shouldn't you have bigger things
to worry about?

15:00.799 --> 15:02.313
Ma'am.

15:02.313 --> 15:03.360
Yeah, Hae Young?

15:03.360 --> 15:05.149
They're replacing all the company cards.

15:05.149 --> 15:07.070
If you give me yours,
I'll dispose of it for you.

15:07.070 --> 15:10.110
- It's in my bag. I'll bring it to you.
- Okay, thanks.

15:25.309 --> 15:27.632
See?

15:27.632 --> 15:30.142
The thing you call impossible...

15:30.142 --> 15:32.407
it's not so impossible after all.

15:53.306 --> 15:56.143
Do we really need to wait
until the next board meeting for this?

15:56.143 --> 15:57.993
It may still be a little premature.

15:57.993 --> 16:01.219
Though of course,
your opinion matters most, sir.

16:02.876 --> 16:05.733
You said you met with MD Han, right?

16:05.733 --> 16:07.002
Yes, I did.

16:18.343 --> 16:20.162
Noh Ki Jun!

16:20.162 --> 16:22.162
Hey, knock first.

16:22.918 --> 16:24.848
I'm making ramen. Want some?

16:24.848 --> 16:26.235
No.

16:26.235 --> 16:27.867
You better not ask for a bite later.

16:27.867 --> 16:29.366
Hey, Ah Jeong.

16:31.088 --> 16:32.865
Your Vice Chairman...

16:32.865 --> 16:34.700
What kind of person is he?

16:36.532 --> 16:38.369
Why are you calling him "your" Vice Chairman?

16:38.369 --> 16:40.740
He's yours too.

16:42.168 --> 16:44.038
Right.

16:44.038 --> 16:45.398
He was my boss.

16:45.398 --> 16:47.581
Why are you suddenly asking about him?

16:47.581 --> 16:51.928
I thought you were stressing over Joo In Ah.

16:51.928 --> 16:54.425
You stormed out
saying you were going to figure out

16:54.425 --> 16:57.178
what was going on between you two.

16:57.877 --> 16:59.120
So? Did you?

16:59.120 --> 17:01.640
I did figure out one thing.

17:02.303 --> 17:04.768
She's insanely hard to read.

17:04.768 --> 17:05.793
What does that mean?

17:05.793 --> 17:07.614
Never mind.

17:07.614 --> 17:09.604
Enjoy your ramen.

17:11.880 --> 17:13.401
What the...

17:36.035 --> 17:38.680
[2025 Haemu Strategic Planning Division
Joint Workshop]

17:53.647 --> 17:55.930
Oh, we're having barbecue?

17:55.930 --> 17:59.220
Yeah, a workshop isn't a workshop
without barbecue.

17:59.220 --> 18:02.444
Team Leader Moo, you've got taste.

18:02.444 --> 18:04.541
Let me help carry some too.

18:04.541 --> 18:05.829
No, this thing's heavy.

18:05.829 --> 18:09.334
Let me show you the charm of
a down-to-earth boss.

18:09.933 --> 18:13.249
This has got to weigh like 20 kilos.
She's so strong.

18:13.249 --> 18:14.630
- Hey, put it down already.
- Okay.

18:14.630 --> 18:16.091
Let's go.

18:24.825 --> 18:27.631
There you go again, acting tough.

18:35.651 --> 18:37.877
[Strategic Planning Division Joint Workshop]

18:37.877 --> 18:39.687
The Planning Office,

18:39.687 --> 18:41.711
HR,

18:41.711 --> 18:43.624
and Audit.

18:44.831 --> 18:48.334
Wow, just hearing those names
sounds intimidating already.

18:50.494 --> 18:53.961
Thank you all for carrying
the weight of this company.

18:53.961 --> 18:56.051
At least during this workshop,

18:56.051 --> 19:00.467
I hope you forget all the work you left behind
and just enjoy yourselves.

19:12.192 --> 19:13.480
Hi, Daddy.

19:13.480 --> 19:14.799
Hold on.

19:14.799 --> 19:18.183
Why are you still awake?
Isn't it almost midnight over there?

19:18.183 --> 19:20.780
I'm tired. Mom nags too much.

19:20.780 --> 19:23.117
Hey, listen to your mom.

19:23.117 --> 19:25.845
She's been getting headaches lately.

19:25.845 --> 19:26.889
Got it?

19:26.889 --> 19:29.121
Go to sleep now. We'll talk again tomorrow.

19:29.121 --> 19:30.183
Good night.

19:30.183 --> 19:32.479
Good night.

19:32.479 --> 19:33.842
Mr. Ahn,

19:33.842 --> 19:35.824
you should take some time off soon

19:35.824 --> 19:38.042
and visit your family in the States.

19:38.042 --> 19:40.262
I didn't realize you were here, sir.

19:40.262 --> 19:41.884
You have a lovely family.

19:41.884 --> 19:43.976
Are the others at the next activity already?

19:43.976 --> 19:47.040
We originally planned some team-building games,

19:47.040 --> 19:51.726
but the two chiefs said
sports are the best way to build teamwork.

19:53.355 --> 19:56.646
[2025 Strategic Planning Division
Joint Workshop]

20:00.015 --> 20:02.155
- Stretch properly.
- Yeah.

20:06.742 --> 20:08.977
I thought we'd just watch
training videos or something.

20:08.977 --> 20:10.467
Why futsal?

20:10.467 --> 20:12.910
Ms. Yoon, didn't you hear?

20:12.910 --> 20:17.026
Ms. Joo said today's MVP
doesn't have to come to work tomorrow.

20:22.623 --> 20:24.409
What are you doing?

20:27.140 --> 20:28.826
Look at her.

20:30.000 --> 20:32.473
Wow, you're really into this.

20:33.761 --> 20:35.559
Faster! Faster!

20:35.559 --> 20:37.965
Guess you don't work out much.

20:38.579 --> 20:40.276
Alright!

20:40.276 --> 20:43.331
It's a co-ed match,
so be careful not to get hurt!

20:43.331 --> 20:46.490
- Got it!
- No sliding tackles!

20:46.490 --> 20:48.492
Let's keep the contact light
and make safety the priority!

20:48.492 --> 20:49.294
Got it!

20:49.294 --> 20:52.813
What does that matter in competition?
Winning's all that counts.

20:52.813 --> 20:54.998
Here, have one before you play.

20:54.998 --> 20:57.035
Time for some energy investing.

20:57.035 --> 20:58.074
Thanks.

20:58.074 --> 20:59.346
- Energy investing?
- Thank you.

20:59.346 --> 21:00.972
Energy's an asset too.

21:00.972 --> 21:04.333
You save it up like investments,
then use it when you need it.

21:04.333 --> 21:06.975
- Thank you.
- Like right now.

21:10.650 --> 21:12.196
Thanks.

21:14.519 --> 21:16.353
Oh, thank you.

21:22.784 --> 21:25.195
Hey, what's going on here?

21:25.195 --> 21:27.313
Why are only your people
getting the good stuff?

21:27.313 --> 21:28.973
Isn't this cheating?

21:28.973 --> 21:31.450
It is, right?

21:31.450 --> 21:32.748
Hello.

21:32.748 --> 21:34.214
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

21:34.214 --> 21:36.159
Hello.

21:36.159 --> 21:37.882
Oh, Vice Chairman.

21:37.882 --> 21:40.755
I thought you left after the welcome speech.

21:40.755 --> 21:43.525
I heard things were getting fun,
so I came to cheer you on.

21:43.525 --> 21:46.312
Then you're rooting for the Audit, right?

21:46.312 --> 21:47.968
What? No way!

21:47.968 --> 21:49.643
You're on HR's side, right?

21:49.643 --> 21:53.400
Well... maybe I'll side with whoever wins.

21:55.621 --> 21:58.051
Then you're on Audit's side.

21:58.051 --> 21:59.957
That's boring.

22:02.892 --> 22:07.171
Isn't it lame to avoid competition
and just side with the stronger team?

22:11.580 --> 22:15.291
You say that like
you're already the stronger one.

22:15.291 --> 22:16.764
Maybe I am.

22:17.770 --> 22:20.443
Because I'm going to win.

22:23.681 --> 22:27.814
Assistant Manager Noh is
a little too competitive sometimes.

22:28.655 --> 22:31.512
Guess we won't be on the same side then.

22:31.512 --> 22:33.902
How about we go head-to-head?

22:33.902 --> 22:36.652
Sir, you're actually playing?

22:36.652 --> 22:38.852
You have a meeting at three.

22:38.852 --> 22:40.745
Cancel it.

23:28.860 --> 23:30.779
Vice Chairman!

23:30.779 --> 23:32.614
Oh no, are you okay?

23:32.614 --> 23:33.907
You alright?

23:33.907 --> 23:36.451
I told you to take it easy! Oh my...

23:36.451 --> 23:39.595
What's with him? Did he lose his mind?

23:39.595 --> 23:42.165
Guess he's trying to win MVP.
So he can skip work tomorrow.

23:42.165 --> 23:44.980
At this rate, he'll be off work forever.

23:44.980 --> 23:46.878
That must be uncomfortable.
Wear my sneakers instead.

23:46.878 --> 23:47.564
It's okay.

23:47.564 --> 23:50.301
- Put these on.
- Thanks.

23:50.918 --> 23:53.662
Better than playing in dress shoes.

24:15.155 --> 24:16.728
What the hell? Hey, foul!

24:16.728 --> 24:18.146
- Ref!
- No foul!

24:18.146 --> 24:20.458
- What?
- No. That wasn't a foul.

24:20.458 --> 24:22.497
That was just physical play.

24:22.497 --> 24:24.749
- Go, go!
- That was excessive...

24:24.749 --> 24:27.085
- Vice Chairman, shoot!
- Hold on, timeout!

24:27.085 --> 24:28.550
Timeout, timeout!

24:28.550 --> 24:31.673
Shoot! Shoot! Shoot!

24:31.673 --> 24:33.594
Timeout! Timeout!

24:33.594 --> 24:37.429
You got that on camera, right? You filmed it.

24:37.429 --> 24:39.139
Ref! VAR! VAR!

24:39.139 --> 24:40.420
Boo, Ki Jun!

24:40.420 --> 24:42.737
Please! VAR!

24:42.737 --> 24:44.811
- VAR please!
- What a sore loser!

24:44.811 --> 24:46.152
Pathetic. So lame.

24:46.152 --> 24:48.258
Playing dirty too.

25:04.998 --> 25:07.711
Alright, back on offense!

25:42.278 --> 25:44.195
You okay?

25:51.772 --> 25:54.297
You were so sure you'd win.

25:54.936 --> 25:56.656
Must be disappointing.

25:57.829 --> 26:00.365
Not really. We didn't exactly play fair.

26:03.410 --> 26:06.626
I'll apologize on In Ah's behalf

26:06.626 --> 26:09.220
for tripping you on purpose.

26:09.220 --> 26:11.709
That's just the kind of person she is.

26:13.733 --> 26:15.913
And what kind of person is that?

26:17.703 --> 26:19.499
Maybe her legs were just too long.

26:20.790 --> 26:23.607
Don't you have someone like that too?

26:23.607 --> 26:26.580
Someone who's always on your side.

26:28.615 --> 26:31.722
In Ah and I go way back.

26:36.463 --> 26:37.976
Sir,

26:38.754 --> 26:40.822
are you feeling guilty about something?

26:41.849 --> 26:44.546
You keep overexplaining yourself.

26:44.546 --> 26:47.650
Makes it seem like
you've got something to hide from me.

27:05.121 --> 27:08.178
Director Choi brought
a change of clothes for you.

27:08.178 --> 27:10.777
Should I adjust your dinner schedule too?

27:12.765 --> 27:14.861
I'm living

27:14.861 --> 27:16.962
with a guy right now.

27:20.343 --> 27:22.343
Secretary Park.

27:23.271 --> 27:26.984
That guy you said you were living with...

27:28.125 --> 27:31.231
Is it Assistant Manager Noh Ki Jun?

27:47.662 --> 27:49.354
Gosh.

27:52.042 --> 27:54.508
Are you going to break it?

27:55.852 --> 27:57.385
Come here.

28:02.895 --> 28:04.307
Sit down.

28:10.653 --> 28:12.892
- Was it this side?
- Gosh, you scared me!

28:15.065 --> 28:17.011
It's this ankle.

28:17.999 --> 28:20.126
- Let me see.
- I'm fine...

28:22.867 --> 28:25.071
It's barely even swollen.

28:25.071 --> 28:26.838
What?

28:26.838 --> 28:29.922
Look.
My ankles are usually way thinner than this.

28:29.922 --> 28:31.624
Such a baby.

28:33.529 --> 28:36.674
First you hurt me, now you're playing nurse?

28:36.674 --> 28:38.769
You tripped me on purpose earlier, huh?

28:38.769 --> 28:40.772
How could you do that to your own teammate?

28:40.772 --> 28:44.406
So what if he missed a goal?
It's not the end of the world.

28:44.406 --> 28:46.430
You must be really worried about him.

28:46.430 --> 28:50.323
If you'd pushed it any further,
your career here would've been over.

28:50.323 --> 28:52.654
In front of all those employees,
especially HR...

28:52.654 --> 28:54.973
Why do you push it so far?

28:54.973 --> 28:58.773
Even if he let it slide,
everyone else would've bowed to him anyway.

29:00.696 --> 29:03.647
You've been in corporate life
long enough to know better.

29:03.647 --> 29:05.692
Why are you acting like a kid?

29:10.521 --> 29:12.411
So you are on my side?

29:12.411 --> 29:14.192
Not the Vice Chairman's?

29:15.078 --> 29:16.608
It's not about sides.

29:16.608 --> 29:20.811
I was just protecting my employee as your boss.

29:30.430 --> 29:31.551
Okay.

29:31.551 --> 29:32.640
What's "okay?"

29:32.640 --> 29:34.715
Your case.

29:34.715 --> 29:36.749
I think I can close it now.

29:36.749 --> 29:37.771
All of a sudden?

29:37.771 --> 29:42.239
When the people involved deny it,
and there's no clear evidence,

29:42.239 --> 29:45.533
these cases usually get closed
without disciplinary action.

29:45.533 --> 29:47.456
I kept wondering if I should dig deeper,

29:47.456 --> 29:51.162
or if I needed to sit down and question

29:51.162 --> 29:53.162
the Vice Chairman himself.

29:55.235 --> 29:57.982
But after today, I think I finally get it.

29:59.182 --> 30:01.499
You two

30:01.499 --> 30:04.262
aren't on the same page at all.

30:08.289 --> 30:09.744
I believe you.

30:11.003 --> 30:12.908
I want to believe

30:14.729 --> 30:16.260
how you feel.

30:20.588 --> 30:22.252
And how exactly

30:23.774 --> 30:25.236
do I feel?

30:29.830 --> 30:32.957
Was today really just about

30:33.586 --> 30:37.142
protecting your employee?

30:44.323 --> 30:47.115
I showed you already.

30:47.115 --> 30:49.354
Nothing's impossible.

30:50.536 --> 30:53.346
I don't care if it takes time.

30:53.346 --> 30:56.359
Take a good look at your feelings.

30:58.032 --> 30:59.971
I'll wait.

31:18.945 --> 31:21.081
So while you were showering,

31:21.081 --> 31:24.341
someone filmed inside the shower room?

31:24.341 --> 31:28.181
Yeah, I'm sure he was filming me with a phone.

31:28.181 --> 31:30.112
Did you see what the guy looked like?

31:30.112 --> 31:32.176
Anything?

31:32.176 --> 31:35.181
I only caught a glimpse of his back,

31:37.811 --> 31:41.083
but he was wearing
our division's men's T-shirt.

31:44.050 --> 31:45.867
Disgusting.

31:47.739 --> 31:49.886
So it was someone from inside.

31:50.766 --> 31:53.230
And since this is the lodging area,
there aren't any security cameras.

31:53.230 --> 31:55.574
Is there anything else you remember?

31:55.574 --> 31:58.464
I think he was using a white phone.

31:58.464 --> 32:02.177
What I saw was white and rectangular.

32:09.160 --> 32:11.170
I think

32:11.170 --> 32:13.640
this could be resolved pretty easily,

32:14.600 --> 32:17.451
if the male employees cooperate.

32:17.451 --> 32:19.057
So you want to check everyone's phones?

32:19.057 --> 32:22.888
Let's only check the phones
belonging to people with white phones.

32:22.888 --> 32:25.605
The suspect could've hidden the phone he used,

32:25.605 --> 32:28.401
so I think we should search all the rooms too.

32:31.064 --> 32:32.445
That's a little much...

32:32.445 --> 32:35.325
I still think we need to verify things first.

32:36.863 --> 32:39.255
I know this is uncomfortable,
but please bear with us.

32:39.255 --> 32:41.546
- Of course.
- We should absolutely do it.

32:41.546 --> 32:44.766
But we can't rule out the possibility
that the suspect is someone from Audit.

32:44.766 --> 32:47.521
So to keep things fair,
let's have one representative from HR

32:47.521 --> 32:49.719
and one from Audit check only what's necessary.

32:49.719 --> 32:51.738
Sounds good.

32:51.738 --> 32:54.342
General Manager Ahn, you can handle it for HR.

32:54.342 --> 32:58.094
If someone like you handles it,
I don't think anyone will complain.

32:58.094 --> 33:00.060
Okay, got it.

33:17.613 --> 33:20.179
- Oh, you...
- Sir, actually...

33:22.101 --> 33:24.411
You two look good together.

33:24.411 --> 33:27.061
- I'll pretend I didn't see anything.
- Thank you.

33:41.073 --> 33:43.270
Come on...

33:43.270 --> 33:46.500
You're with Audit. How can you be doing this?

33:54.953 --> 33:56.713
This is...

33:57.912 --> 34:00.845
This is leftover sauce from the barbecue...

34:04.157 --> 34:07.254
No, let's just give it to him.
It's already been opened anyway.

34:07.254 --> 34:09.254
Take it home and eat it.

34:10.567 --> 34:11.960
Thanks.

34:22.897 --> 34:25.808
Just in case,
we checked all the women's rooms too,

34:25.808 --> 34:27.531
but nothing turned up.

34:27.531 --> 34:30.156
Still, we should do everything we can.

34:32.314 --> 34:35.105
Maybe there are security cameras
near the entrance?

34:35.105 --> 34:36.469
Once it gets light tomorrow,

34:36.469 --> 34:39.591
I'll ask the Operations Team
and check right away.

34:39.591 --> 34:42.009
Anyway, everyone worked hard tonight.

34:42.009 --> 34:44.114
Let's all get some rest.

34:44.114 --> 34:45.887
Good work, everyone.

34:49.832 --> 34:51.022
Mr. Ahn,

34:51.022 --> 34:52.770
you dropped this.

34:55.883 --> 34:57.413
You smoke?

34:57.413 --> 34:58.919
Since when?

35:00.226 --> 35:01.696
Yeah, just occasionally.

35:01.696 --> 35:03.417
I keep it on the down-low.

35:03.417 --> 35:06.284
Why are you sneaking cigarettes even at work?

35:06.284 --> 35:08.494
Want to step outside for a smoke together?

35:08.494 --> 35:11.254
I think he was using a white phone.

35:11.254 --> 35:13.444
No, it's okay. I'm quitting soon anyway.

35:13.444 --> 35:15.399
Thanks. Give it here.

35:15.399 --> 35:17.486
- I'm not giving it back.
- Why not?

35:17.486 --> 35:19.696
If you're really quitting,
you should start now.

35:19.696 --> 35:20.925
I'll help you out.

35:20.925 --> 35:23.574
No, I'll quit starting tomorrow.

35:23.574 --> 35:25.466
Stuff like this only works
if you quit cold turkey.

35:25.466 --> 35:27.972
Mr. Noh, don't give it back.

35:27.972 --> 35:29.210
Yes, ma'am.

35:29.210 --> 35:31.341
Come on, you guys are ruthless.

35:31.341 --> 35:32.739
Just give it back already!

35:32.739 --> 35:36.045
Seriously.
Why are you messing with the man's cigarettes?

35:36.045 --> 35:37.947
Those things are expensive now.

35:37.947 --> 35:39.327
Exactly.

35:39.932 --> 35:41.593
Yeah?

36:01.489 --> 36:03.088
What the...

36:04.396 --> 36:08.008
What? What is it?

36:09.944 --> 36:12.579
Isn't this a camera?

36:15.372 --> 36:17.170
Mr. Ahn!

36:17.170 --> 36:19.174
Jesus Christ.

36:22.260 --> 36:25.193
You've lost your mind!

36:34.061 --> 36:37.215
You really went all out.

36:37.215 --> 36:40.221
Anytime, anywhere, huh?

36:40.221 --> 36:42.031
From the elevator on the way to work,

36:42.031 --> 36:45.085
to the office cafeteria, the bathroom,

36:45.085 --> 36:47.211
even the subway ride home.

36:48.578 --> 36:50.281
How did you even take this one...

36:53.171 --> 36:54.498
No way.

36:54.498 --> 36:58.118
Did you install cameras under employees' desks?

36:58.118 --> 37:00.242
This angle is way too low.

37:00.242 --> 37:01.868
Ma'am, you know...

37:01.868 --> 37:06.352
How could you do this to people
you see every single day?

37:06.352 --> 37:09.070
What the hell do you even think
your coworkers are?

37:09.070 --> 37:11.350
Okay, I get it, but...

37:12.223 --> 37:14.633
Everyone's cooperating, aren't they?

37:14.633 --> 37:18.397
Making a huge scene out of this
won't help the company either.

37:18.397 --> 37:20.733
There's already the issue
with suspicion falling on our division,

37:20.733 --> 37:23.486
- and the company's image...
- Right. That's important.

37:23.486 --> 37:26.322
The division's reputation. The company's image.

37:26.322 --> 37:28.018
Which is exactly why...

37:33.739 --> 37:35.763
we should make an example out of this.

37:35.763 --> 37:38.236
Then this is the perfect chance
to prove we're better

37:38.236 --> 37:42.700
than those companies that cover up

37:42.700 --> 37:44.646
workplace sex crimes.

38:02.705 --> 38:04.603
Today...

38:04.603 --> 38:07.349
I'm eating at the cafeteria.

38:07.956 --> 38:10.492
Okay, I'll let them know.

38:10.492 --> 38:12.422
No.

38:12.422 --> 38:14.584
Let's just head down now.

38:18.965 --> 38:21.003
I told you, I don't eat cafeteria food.

38:21.003 --> 38:24.149
Just eat already so we can wrap up
General Manager Ahn's report.

38:24.149 --> 38:25.298
Eat.

38:25.298 --> 38:28.010
Come on, good food boosts productivity.

38:28.010 --> 38:30.041
That's how you get good reports.

38:31.197 --> 38:33.201
It's good though.

38:33.201 --> 38:34.642
It's tasty.

38:41.558 --> 38:43.126
What the...

38:45.716 --> 38:47.650
Mind if I join you?

38:48.536 --> 38:51.026
Sure. It's not like we reserved the place.

38:51.026 --> 38:52.626
Have a seat.

39:05.853 --> 39:07.381
Jae Yeol went to the cafeteria?

39:07.381 --> 39:08.441
Yes.

39:08.441 --> 39:12.516
And he sat with our Head of Audit
and Mr. Noh from Audit Team 3.

39:12.516 --> 39:15.095
The whole Audit is freaking out.

39:16.223 --> 39:20.540
Man, my brother's sneakier than he looks.

39:20.540 --> 39:23.366
Well, I've got Audit Team 1's finest, huh?

39:23.366 --> 39:25.366
I've got you on my side.

39:27.049 --> 39:29.543
I'm honored, sir.

39:30.647 --> 39:32.281
So how's work these days?

39:32.281 --> 39:34.805
You're handling affiliate audits now, right?

39:34.805 --> 39:38.085
Yes, I'm currently in charge
of Steel and Pharma.

39:40.360 --> 39:42.798
Oh, you're handling Pharma?

39:42.798 --> 39:45.437
Who was in charge before you?

39:47.014 --> 39:51.286
May I ask why you're asking?

39:51.286 --> 39:53.969
Oh, it's nothing serious.

39:53.969 --> 39:56.429
I had drinks with some people
from Pharma yesterday,

39:56.429 --> 39:59.399
and they said HQ Audit
used to be all over them,

39:59.399 --> 40:02.271
but things have gone quiet lately.

40:02.271 --> 40:05.214
So I was wondering
if the old team was power-tripping,

40:05.214 --> 40:08.747
or if things just weren't being handled
properly now.

40:08.747 --> 40:10.905
Guess it was because
the person in charge changed.

40:10.905 --> 40:12.405
I see.

40:22.218 --> 40:24.789
I heard you played a big role

40:24.789 --> 40:26.968
in catching the illegal filming suspect.

40:26.968 --> 40:29.868
Well, I was just doing my job.

40:30.511 --> 40:34.130
Seems like a capable employee.
So why are you wasting him on PM work?

40:37.930 --> 40:41.734
I'm good at pretty much everything.

40:47.513 --> 40:49.086
This is good.

41:20.662 --> 41:22.985
You two...

41:22.985 --> 41:25.825
are close, aren't you?

41:25.825 --> 41:28.230
I happened to see you together

41:28.230 --> 41:31.176
when I dropped her off the other day.

41:32.693 --> 41:34.361
Is it rude to bring up
personal matters like this

41:34.361 --> 41:37.448
in front of your direct supervisor?

41:37.448 --> 41:39.672
Yes. It is rude.

41:42.103 --> 41:43.704
And what's wrong with it anyway?

41:43.704 --> 41:45.370
Housing prices in Seoul are insane.

41:45.370 --> 41:47.030
It's economical.

41:48.038 --> 41:50.188
You knew about this?

41:50.188 --> 41:51.761
Of course.

41:52.491 --> 41:55.878
Head Joo's even been to our place before.

42:00.043 --> 42:01.503
Really?

42:04.860 --> 42:09.020
Since when did this company
start doing home visits?

42:18.275 --> 42:21.798
I should probably get going.

42:21.798 --> 42:23.768
I was in the middle of something.

42:23.768 --> 42:25.556
Sit down.

42:25.556 --> 42:27.499
We sat at the same table.

42:27.499 --> 42:30.299
Isn't it rude to leave first?

42:32.718 --> 42:34.688
The Vice Chairman's right.

42:34.688 --> 42:36.315
Let's go together, Mr. Noh.

42:36.315 --> 42:38.998
I almost let you leave alone. How rude of me.

42:38.998 --> 42:42.357
We were eating together originally.

42:42.357 --> 42:44.223
Then enjoy your meal, you two.

42:44.223 --> 42:45.645
Let's go.

42:47.612 --> 42:49.744
Come on, hurry up.

43:01.984 --> 43:04.868
- This is good, right?
- Yeah.

43:04.868 --> 43:08.091
I hate wasting food, but it couldn't be helped.

43:08.091 --> 43:10.048
Such a waste.

43:10.048 --> 43:12.468
By the way, this toast is amazing.

43:12.468 --> 43:15.965
First time trying it?
That place has been famous forever.

43:15.965 --> 43:17.269
Back when I was a rookie,

43:17.269 --> 43:19.294
buying one of these on the way to work
and eating it at my desk

43:19.294 --> 43:21.345
was the highlight of my day.

43:21.345 --> 43:23.765
Did you buy one for the Vice Chairman too?

43:23.765 --> 43:25.315
Who knows?

43:28.206 --> 43:31.190
He must've been pissed. Right?

43:31.190 --> 43:34.290
How am I supposed to survive at work now?

43:34.970 --> 43:37.934
Are you going to take responsibility
and protect your employee?

43:37.934 --> 43:40.713
Who told you to act out like that?

43:40.713 --> 43:44.873
Come on,
the Vice Chairman was being ridiculously petty.

43:45.859 --> 43:47.411
Anyway, after today,

43:47.411 --> 43:50.122
it's pretty obvious he's still not over you.

43:50.122 --> 43:52.124
Want to reopen the investigation then?

43:52.124 --> 43:53.176
No.

43:53.176 --> 43:55.428
As long as you're not the problem,
I don't care.

43:56.254 --> 43:58.297
Some people just hold onto their first love.

43:58.297 --> 44:01.573
Like the rose from The Little Prince.

44:04.306 --> 44:07.348
- What's that supposed to mean?
- You know...

44:07.348 --> 44:11.677
Even after the Little Prince comes to Earth
and sees all those identical roses,

44:11.677 --> 44:15.517
he still goes back to the planet with his rose.

44:16.468 --> 44:18.959
The Little Prince goes back?

44:18.959 --> 44:20.361
Doesn't he stay on Earth with the fox?

44:20.361 --> 44:23.263
No, he goes back.

44:23.263 --> 44:25.157
He says he has to take responsibility
for the rose he raised.

44:25.157 --> 44:27.280
No, he stays on Earth.

44:27.280 --> 44:28.955
No, he goes back.

44:28.955 --> 44:30.606
Want to bet on it?

44:31.227 --> 44:32.378
A bet?

44:32.378 --> 44:33.415
Deal.

44:33.415 --> 44:36.129
But no wish bet. Loser gets punished.

44:36.129 --> 44:37.195
Fine.

44:37.840 --> 44:40.241
"I'll be going back to my star tonight."

44:40.241 --> 44:42.907
See? He goes back to his planet.

44:44.288 --> 44:46.640
What the heck? This is actually really sad.

44:46.640 --> 44:49.523
Why did I remember it as a happy ending?

44:49.523 --> 44:52.717
Guess you just interpreted it
as a happy ending back then.

44:53.310 --> 44:54.770
If he made it all the way to Earth,

44:54.770 --> 44:57.115
why go through all that trouble
just to leave again?

45:00.161 --> 45:01.756
So I win, right?

45:02.372 --> 45:06.171
Hey, you really took
children's books seriously, huh?

45:07.000 --> 45:10.933
Just admit defeat gracefully
and take your punishment.

45:11.651 --> 45:14.782
Fine, I admit it. What's the punishment?

45:14.782 --> 45:16.038
Okay.

45:17.076 --> 45:19.353
Now what should we do here

45:19.353 --> 45:21.905
to turn this into a tragic fairy tale?

45:33.600 --> 45:35.600
What are you plotting?

45:55.122 --> 45:57.765
Head Joo finally put something in her hair.

46:03.273 --> 46:05.226
Ma'am...

46:07.200 --> 46:08.944
Your hair...

46:11.719 --> 46:13.351
What?

46:14.766 --> 46:16.769
Isn't it cute?

46:16.769 --> 46:19.691
I'm totally obsessed
with stuff like this lately.

46:25.867 --> 46:27.927
Alright, show's over.

46:43.096 --> 46:45.231
[Art Class Director]

46:49.836 --> 46:51.279
Thank you.

46:51.279 --> 46:52.724
That's cute.

46:52.724 --> 46:55.344
What's with the hairpin?

46:55.344 --> 46:58.336
Oh right. I still had this on?

46:59.056 --> 47:00.714
This is so embarrassing.

47:00.714 --> 47:02.210
Well, that's unusual.

47:02.210 --> 47:03.650
Is it trendy these days?

47:03.650 --> 47:07.033
No, someone just gave it to me.

47:07.659 --> 47:09.452
It's a punishment.

47:12.820 --> 47:14.308
Anyway,

47:14.897 --> 47:17.234
you're saying I shouldn't model anymore?

47:17.234 --> 47:18.774
What, am I fired?

47:18.774 --> 47:21.552
We should really be using pro models now.

47:21.552 --> 47:25.471
I've been shamelessly using you
because of budget issues.

47:25.471 --> 47:29.194
Oh, come on. I did it because I wanted to.

47:29.194 --> 47:32.281
And you know that. I needed this.

47:32.281 --> 47:34.379
Do you still?

47:36.780 --> 47:40.251
I've known you a long time, In Ah.

47:40.251 --> 47:41.481
Lately, I've been thinking

47:41.481 --> 47:45.897
maybe you don't need this place
as much anymore.

47:46.794 --> 47:48.459
You've been smiling a lot.

47:49.884 --> 47:51.194
- Me?
- Yeah.

47:51.194 --> 47:53.194
You seem relaxed.

47:53.797 --> 47:55.447
Tell me.

47:55.447 --> 47:57.248
There's someone, isn't there?

47:57.248 --> 47:59.500
The guy who gave you that pin?

48:02.093 --> 48:05.085
No, this is just...

48:05.085 --> 48:06.873
Since you're the flower of our Audit Team,

48:06.873 --> 48:08.265
how about adding an actual flower?

48:08.265 --> 48:09.857
Here.

48:11.677 --> 48:13.325
Pig.

48:13.325 --> 48:15.814
And rabbit.

48:15.814 --> 48:17.763
Look to the side.

48:21.450 --> 48:22.662
I can't do that.

48:22.662 --> 48:25.328
What do you mean, you can't?

48:26.298 --> 48:28.357
He works at my company.

48:29.375 --> 48:33.635
There's a saying overseas about office dating.

48:33.635 --> 48:36.154
"Don't crap where you eat."

48:37.502 --> 48:39.172
That's how crazy it is.

48:39.172 --> 48:41.022
So what?

48:41.022 --> 48:43.169
Isn't that better than bottling everything up?

48:43.169 --> 48:47.079
What's wrong with doing
something a little crazy?

48:47.079 --> 48:51.247
Before you started modeling,
didn't you think this was crazy too?

48:51.247 --> 48:52.636
But once you tried it,

48:52.636 --> 48:55.764
it became the one escape
from your everyday life.

48:55.764 --> 48:58.090
Don't box yourself in.

48:58.090 --> 48:59.765
Once you step outside those limits,

48:59.765 --> 49:02.228
that's when new happiness finds you.

49:04.013 --> 49:06.456
Wow, you sound wise today.

49:06.456 --> 49:08.589
You just realized?

49:31.759 --> 49:34.640
[Art Class Today: 9 PM]

49:49.821 --> 49:52.207
Was I this pretty?

50:04.495 --> 50:07.128
Yeah, you are.

50:31.276 --> 50:33.868
[Audit Report]

50:39.043 --> 50:41.347
You barely touched your lunch.

50:41.347 --> 50:43.099
Please eat something.

50:44.383 --> 50:45.860
Okay.

50:45.860 --> 50:48.370
And you went too far earlier.

50:50.536 --> 50:53.340
You totally used me.

50:53.340 --> 50:55.465
I know

50:55.465 --> 50:57.909
you like Head Joo.

51:00.343 --> 51:03.662
I'm a very capable secretary.

51:03.662 --> 51:06.094
I'm also a woman who likes you.

51:08.178 --> 51:10.203
Ki Jun is...

51:10.203 --> 51:12.422
a really great guy.

51:13.394 --> 51:17.352
For the first time in my life,
I hated someone seeing me at my worst,

51:17.352 --> 51:20.488
and ran away
because I didn't want to burden him.

51:20.488 --> 51:23.626
I didn't want to look pathetic in front of him.

51:31.431 --> 51:33.015
Why are you telling me this?

51:33.015 --> 51:36.268
Because that's how impossible it is.
For you to beat Ki Jun.

51:37.700 --> 51:39.823
Even if you are the Vice Chairman.

51:57.779 --> 52:00.855
[Report Regarding
U.S. Assignment Personnel Changes]

52:16.421 --> 52:18.758
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

52:18.758 --> 52:20.465
- Two toast sandwiches, please.
- Sure.

52:20.465 --> 52:22.465
- Please make them good.
- Of course.

52:24.139 --> 52:26.934
- Enjoy your food.
- Thank you.

52:32.930 --> 52:34.895
Beats me.

52:34.895 --> 52:36.651
What could he possibly have left to say?

52:36.651 --> 52:38.334
[General Manager Ahn (Pervert)]

52:44.586 --> 52:47.981
The person you're calling is unavailable.
Please leave a message...

52:47.981 --> 52:49.243
[Assistant Manager Noh Ki Jun]

52:55.221 --> 52:57.207
Come on, pick up.

53:12.407 --> 53:14.005
Hey, Noh Ki Jun!

53:14.005 --> 53:15.437
What are you, seriously?

53:15.437 --> 53:17.697
You really got yourself
on the Vice Chairman's good side, huh?

53:17.697 --> 53:19.029
What are you talking about?

53:19.029 --> 53:20.839
I heard it all from HR.

53:20.839 --> 53:22.955
You're getting sent to the U.S., right?

53:24.032 --> 53:25.189
What?

53:26.325 --> 53:27.944
Lucky you.

53:30.945 --> 53:33.925
The person you're calling is unavailable...

53:37.904 --> 53:40.456
Assistant Manager Lee.

53:40.456 --> 53:43.022
Thanks for coming out even though you're busy.

53:49.779 --> 53:51.917
You're putting me in a difficult position too.

53:51.917 --> 53:54.426
You know I'm in deep trouble right now.

53:54.426 --> 53:56.468
My wife is about to divorce me.

53:56.468 --> 53:58.321
She says...

54:00.440 --> 54:03.446
I can forget about ever seeing my son again.

54:05.079 --> 54:06.196
Please...

54:06.196 --> 54:07.702
Help me.

54:07.702 --> 54:11.907
Can't you help me get a lighter punishment?

54:11.907 --> 54:16.330
Tell them I worked hard all these years,
that I had a good reputation.

54:16.330 --> 54:19.603
Maybe get the employees
to write petitions for me too.

54:19.603 --> 54:23.240
Even if I wanted to help personally,

54:23.240 --> 54:26.049
Audit's taking this really seriously.

54:26.049 --> 54:27.474
You know...

54:27.474 --> 54:31.264
I've been trying to get ahold
of Assistant Manager Noh too,

54:31.264 --> 54:33.503
but he won't answer.

54:34.204 --> 54:35.414
Sir,

54:35.414 --> 54:37.479
he's riding high right now.

54:37.479 --> 54:39.945
He got recognized because of your case,
he's getting promoted,

54:39.945 --> 54:42.381
and now he's even going to the U.S. assignment.

54:43.136 --> 54:45.136
You didn't know?

54:46.563 --> 54:48.014
Director Park,

54:48.014 --> 54:50.441
I heard your daughter's getting married.

54:50.441 --> 54:52.071
Congratulations.

54:52.071 --> 54:54.311
Let me know once the date's set.

54:54.311 --> 54:55.821
I'd love to give a speech.

54:55.821 --> 54:58.891
Wow, that wedding's going to be huge.

54:58.891 --> 55:00.003
Oh my...

55:00.003 --> 55:04.190
You'd personally attend and even give a speech?

55:04.190 --> 55:06.926
Or should I sing instead?

55:25.700 --> 55:28.397
The person you're calling is unavailable...

55:28.397 --> 55:29.650
Why isn't she answering?

55:29.650 --> 55:30.790
[Joo In Ah]

55:34.936 --> 55:37.059
The person you're calling is unavailable...

55:39.224 --> 55:42.123
Hey, have you seen Head Joo?

55:42.890 --> 55:44.567
I'm asking if you've seen her.

55:44.567 --> 55:47.621
I didn't see it myself,
but Seung Hee just told me.

55:47.621 --> 55:51.012
Head Joo suddenly showed up,
then left with the Vice Chairman.

55:52.149 --> 55:53.548
Where'd they go?

55:57.206 --> 55:58.837
- What are you trying to do?
- What do you mean?

55:58.837 --> 56:00.370
About Noh Ki Jun.

56:00.370 --> 56:03.550
How do you ship him off overnight

56:03.550 --> 56:05.170
without even giving us a heads-up?

56:05.170 --> 56:07.688
What is he, some kind of package?

56:07.688 --> 56:11.561
So that's why you barged in here?

56:12.207 --> 56:14.366
In the middle of an executive meeting?

56:14.366 --> 56:16.335
Over one assistant manager?

56:16.335 --> 56:18.093
This isn't just about him.

56:18.093 --> 56:21.335
This is about respecting my role and authority.

56:21.335 --> 56:25.431
How do you transfer someone
with zero disciplinary issues like this?

56:27.299 --> 56:29.542
This is completely unfair.

56:29.542 --> 56:31.813
Honestly, it's audit-worthy.

56:31.813 --> 56:33.696
I reviewed everything.

56:33.696 --> 56:37.181
A capable employee with great results
doing nothing but PM work?

56:37.181 --> 56:39.181
That's a loss for the company.

56:41.428 --> 56:43.428
That's really the reason?

56:44.726 --> 56:47.241
This has nothing to do with personal feelings?

56:48.132 --> 56:49.496
It's a U.S. assignment.

56:49.496 --> 56:52.289
Every employee wants a posting like that.

56:52.289 --> 56:54.519
For someone at his level,
it's basically special treatment.

56:54.519 --> 56:56.637
He's getting promoted to manager too.

56:56.637 --> 56:59.080
Is this really worth getting upset over?

56:59.080 --> 57:00.450
Or are you the one

57:00.450 --> 57:05.389
letting personal feelings
hold back a promising employee's career?

57:06.324 --> 57:08.687
Can you honestly say

57:08.687 --> 57:11.660
you're upset for purely professional reasons?

57:16.348 --> 57:18.535
In Ah.

57:18.535 --> 57:21.135
I had a lot of options.

57:22.001 --> 57:25.864
And I chose the most considerate one.

57:33.454 --> 57:35.527
The person you're calling is unavailable...

57:36.994 --> 57:38.666
Noh Ki Jun.

57:42.217 --> 57:43.763
Mr. Ahn?

57:45.737 --> 57:48.927
You can't keep showing up like this
and calling me...

57:55.723 --> 57:57.723
You bastard...

59:13.037 --> 59:16.150
You can't drive like this. I'll take you.

59:33.604 --> 59:35.984
So they're still waiting at the ER?

59:39.148 --> 59:41.878
No, you don't have to. I'll call again later.

59:41.878 --> 59:43.928
Just let me out here.

59:43.928 --> 59:46.119
You're still pretty far.
Just past the intersection...

59:46.119 --> 59:48.897
In Ah... In Ah!

01:00:04.382 --> 01:00:06.628
It just hurts.

01:00:10.462 --> 01:00:12.641
Feels like you must've been really lonely.

01:00:15.325 --> 01:00:17.853
You keep acting tough,

01:00:19.654 --> 01:00:22.040
and that just makes it sadder.

01:00:26.998 --> 01:00:30.318
But let me ask you one thing.

01:00:38.155 --> 01:00:40.968
Why are you pushing me away this hard?

01:00:53.732 --> 01:00:56.344
That question you asked me...

01:00:57.184 --> 01:01:00.371
Why I really keep pushing you away...

01:01:04.654 --> 01:01:06.092
I...

01:01:09.441 --> 01:01:10.952
I...

01:01:46.311 --> 01:01:47.352
Mr. Noh...

01:01:47.352 --> 01:01:49.075
I was scared. It scared me.

01:01:49.075 --> 01:01:52.496
You can go with us
on the Jeju business trip next week.

01:01:52.496 --> 01:01:53.759
What the hell are you doing?

01:01:53.759 --> 01:01:56.416
You sent him overseas because of your feelings.

01:01:56.416 --> 01:01:58.923
In Ah, just stay by my side.

01:01:58.923 --> 01:02:02.060
Why did you really send me to Team 3?

01:02:02.060 --> 01:02:03.650
Because you were afraid he might get hurt?

01:02:03.650 --> 01:02:06.150
None of this makes any sense to me.

01:02:06.150 --> 01:02:08.407
Talk to me. Right now.

01:02:08.407 --> 01:02:09.677
I'm weird like that.

01:02:09.677 --> 01:02:13.337
When it really matters, I hide how I feel.
